  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:mixture-of-experts",
  "domain": "machine-learning",
  "definition": "A sparse neural network architecture in which a learned router (gating network) dispatches each input \u2014 in modern transformers, each token at each MoE layer \u2014 to a small subset of many parallel expert sub-networks, so that total parameter count can grow enormously while per-token computation stays roughly constant; introduced by Jacobs and Jordan in 1991 and revived at scale by Shazeer's sparsely-gated MoE and the Switch Transformer, it underpins frontier models such as Mixtral and DeepSeek-V3.",
